# --- Secrets ------------------------------------------------------------
# This repository is PUBLIC. Nothing here may ever contain a real credential.
# Real values live outside the repo; only .example files are tracked.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
!**/testdata/**/*.key
secrets/
secrets-generated/

# --- Real content -------------------------------------------------------
# This repository is PUBLIC, and a credential is not the only thing that must never
# reach it. `content-darm/` is the owner's personal medical reference about a child;
# committing it would publish health data about a named family to the world, and no
# secret scanner would object, because health data is not credential-shaped.
#
# `content-example/` IS tracked, deliberately — it is invented demonstration text with
# no real person in it. The distinction is the point: what makes content unpublishable
# here is whose life it describes, not which directory it sits in. Anything imported
# from the owner's notes belongs on this side of the line.
content-darm/

# --- Build artefacts ----------------------------------------------------
/target
**/target
/web/build
/web/.svelte-kit
/web/node_modules
node_modules/
/extension/dist
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- Runtime / derived state -------------------------------------------
# The database, search index, vectors and blobs are DERIVED. They are
# rebuildable from the content export and must never be committed.
/data
/media
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# --- Agent tooling ------------------------------------------------------
# .serena/project.yml IS tracked (it is config); the cache under it is not.
.serena/cache/
.serena/memories/
graphify-out/
GRAPH_TREE.html
GRAPH_*.html
.playwright-mcp/
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/

# --- OS / editor --------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/
!.vscode/extensions.json
.mutate-backups/
